# ShoeFit - New Feature Proposals

## Overview

This document outlines additional features to enhance ShoeFit's value proposition, increase user engagement, and drive retention. These features build upon the existing foot scanning, recommendation, and wishlist systems while introducing new dimensions of social engagement, purchase intelligence, and health integration.

---

## New Features

### 9. Price Tracking & Deal Alerts

**Screen:** New tab or integrated into Wishlist (`/deals` or enhanced `/wishlist`)

A price monitoring system that tracks wishlist items across retailers and notifies users when prices drop.

- **Price History Charts:** Interactive line chart showing historical price data for each shoe across retailers (StockX, GOAT, Flight Club, official brand sites).
- **Target Price Setting:** Users can set a "buy it now" price threshold for any wishlist item with a slider or numeric input.
- **Push Notifications:** Background price checking with local/push notifications when:
  - Price drops below target threshold
  - Flash sales or limited-time deals detected
  - New lowest price in 30/60/90 days
- **Deal Score Badge:** AI-calculated "deal score" (1-100) displayed on shoe cards indicating how good the current price is relative to historical averages and retail price.
- **Price Comparison View:** Side-by-side retailer price comparison with shipping estimates and authenticity guarantees.
- **Restock Alerts:** Notifications when out-of-stock sizes become available, prioritizing user's recommended size.
- **Deal Feed:** Chronological feed of price drops across all wishlisted items with quick "Buy Now" actions.
- **Haptic Feedback:** Success notification haptics when setting price alerts.

**Data Requirements:**
- New `priceAlerts` array in UserContext with: shoeId, targetPrice, isActive, notificationsSent
- New `priceHistory` cache with daily price snapshots per shoe/retailer
- Background fetch task registration for periodic price checks

