### 12. AR Try-On Experience

**Screen:** Full-screen modal from shoe detail (`/ar-tryon`)

Augmented reality feature allowing users to visualize shoes on their feet using the device camera.

- **Live Camera Feed:** Real-time AR overlay of 3D shoe model positioned on user's feet.
- **Foot Detection:** ML-powered foot detection using the device camera to anchor the virtual shoe accurately.
- **Multiple Angles:** Users can view the shoe from front, side, and back by repositioning their feet.
- **Color Switching:** Tap to instantly switch colorways within the AR view.
- **Size Simulation:** Visual representation of how the shoe would look in different sizes (helpful for deciding whether to size up/down).
- **Capture & Share:** Take photo or video of AR try-on; share directly to social media or save to camera roll.
- **Lighting Adaptation:** AR shoe rendering adapts to ambient lighting conditions for realistic appearance.
- **Comparison Mode:** Split-screen showing two colorways or two different shoes side-by-side in AR.
- **Wishlist Shortcut:** Add to wishlist directly from AR view.

**Technical Requirements:**
- Integration with ARKit (iOS) and ARCore (Android) via expo-ar or custom native module
- 3D shoe model assets (USDZ for iOS, GLTF for Android) linked to shoe catalog
- ML foot detection model (potentially Core ML / TensorFlow Lite)

